**Day 27: SQLite CRUD & Python Integration**  

**Topic:**  
SQLite CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations and integrating SQLite with Python using the `sqlite3` module.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand SQLite CRUD operations  
• Learn to connect SQLite with Python  
• Write Python scripts to create tables, insert, and query data  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Execute SQLite CRUD operations via Python  
• Develop a Python script to interact with an SQLite database  
• Practice querying and manipulating data  

**Important Concepts:**  
• SQLite as a lightweight, serverless database  
• Parameterized queries for security  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `CREATE TABLE table_name (column1 datatype, ...)`  
• `INSERT INTO table_name VALUES (value1, ...)`  
• `SELECT * FROM table_name`  
• `UPDATE table_name SET column = value WHERE condition`  
• `DELETE FROM table_name WHERE condition`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Local data storage for mobile apps  
• Prototyping database-driven applications  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• SQLite  
• Python 3  
• VS Code  

**Summary:**  
Learned SQLite CRUD operations and Python integration using `sqlite3`. Practiced creating tables, inserting, updating, and querying data via Python scripts.  

